# Database schema

- PostgreSQL 16 + Prisma 6 via `DATABASE_URL`. Follow the always-on identifier standard in `05-record-identifiers.mdc`: internal BIGINT PK/FKs plus immutable random UUIDv4 public_id on every table. Active Prisma still uses legacy cuid() until #33 adopts the SQL target; do not treat that legacy shape as the standard for new target work.
- Use `Asia/Bangkok` as the timezone for all persisted dates and timestamps. Date-only values represent Bangkok calendar dates; timestamp columns represent Bangkok local wall-clock values. Configure the PostgreSQL session timezone to `Asia/Bangkok` for database-generated defaults and use explicit application conversions; never normalize persisted values to UTC.
- `WorkItem` maps to table `work_items`. Active legacy field `types` maps to `labels_types` (`String[]`); SQL target uses type_labels per dictionary.
- Target: multiple Companies + `Project.companyId` (nullable only during Dhas backfill, then NOT NULL). No Customer model.
- Target integrations: external_project_mappings unique(provider, instance_url, external_project_id); external_work_item_references unique(provider, instance_url, external_project_id, external_issue_id) and unique(work_item_id). Local relations use numeric IDs; local client references use public UUIDs. Never store tokens in tables.
- TimeEntry workflow requires `workItemId`. `projectId` must match the WorkItem. Schema today allows nulls and does not enforce the pair — close this in API now, DB when ready.
- Set Decimal precision. Retain current DECIMAL(65,30) for hours/budget/spending. Validate positive hours/progress in services; add DB checks only after reviewing existing rows.
- Do not put Developer/Infra/SA on `User.role`. Reserve unique Company code `dhas` for the default existing-Project backfill. `ProjectMember` stays unused by product.
- Current Project/WorkItem delete guards and restrictive relations preserve history; never infer cascade behavior from an older backup. Review archive/soft-delete policy before any change.
- Indexes from real queries (`projectId+status`, `role+status`, `TimeEntry(date)`, `companyId+status`). Measure first.
- Rollout: backup + restore test → additive nullable → backfill → validate → NOT NULL/unique. Active legacy runtime uses guarded db-push-safe until #33; SQL target uses its versioned runner after compatible adoption.
- If multiple User rows exist, pick the owner with audit. Do not delete user rows until every FK is remapped.
